preConditionHook:
// THE DAY IS A TREND DAY AND ITS DIRECTION IS UP (long side): once at least
// openingBars bars of the session have printed, the close sits at least
// trendDayAtr ATRs above the session's OPENING price. While that holds, only
// with-trend entries are permitted for the rest of the session; the short
// side is the mirror below the open.
//
// TP4-07 is the cleanest of the three sources -- "the sign of close minus
// session open once the opening range has printed" -- and wins over R08-24's
// alternative (a fraction of the session's bars closed on one side of the
// EMA) and over TP4-08, which adds no test of its own.
//
// NOT MorningLegDirection, although both measure close minus session open at
// the same default bar count. That rule LATCHES its answer at exactly
// firstHourBars and holds it for the rest of the day, which is what makes it
// a day-TYPE flag; this one is re-evaluated on EVERY bar from openingBars on,
// so it goes false the moment price comes back to the open and true again
// when it leaves. The two disagree on every day whose morning leg is given
// back. Not the always-in direction either: this resets every session and
// reads the session open, where always-in is continuous across the whole
// series, and the two disagree on any gap day. Not
// TrendDayIdentifiedInFirstHour, which measures from the opening RANGE
// against that range's own height.
//
// The ATR is MultiWalk's WFSafe_AvgTrueRange, ONE CALL SITE, advanced
// UNCONDITIONALLY before the conditions are read: it is a rolling accumulator
// and must step exactly once per bar, so it can never sit inside an if.
// Ported from AtrProfitTarget -- seeded with a full sum on the first
// calculated bar or when the length changes, thereafter TWO statements,
// because EL evaluates S[1] + in - out left to right.
//
// SESSION MODEL, per the standing decision: the twin's date > date[1],
// mirrored as day_of(ctx.Time(0)) > day_of(ctx.Time(1)); barsIn is 1 on the
// session's first bar, the corpus convention. Intraday bars only. WARM-UP
// mirrors EL: barsIn and sessOpen hold their initial 0 if the first
// calculated bar falls mid-session.
//
// Deepest bar touched: atrLookback + 1.
if (day_of(ctx.Time(0)) > day_of(ctx.Time(1))) {
    barsIn = 1;
    sessOpen = open[0];
} else {
    barsIn = barsIn + 1;
}
if (atrLen != (int)atrLookback) {
    atrSum = 0.0;
    for (int i = 0; i < (int)atrLookback; ++i) {
        double hi = high[i] > close[i + 1] ? high[i] : close[i + 1];
        double lo = low[i] < close[i + 1] ? low[i] : close[i + 1];
        atrSum += hi - lo;
    }
    atrLen = (int)atrLookback;
} else {
    const int out = (int)atrLookback;
    double hiIn = high[0] > close[1] ? high[0] : close[1];
    double loIn = low[0] < close[1] ? low[0] : close[1];
    double hiOut = high[out] > close[out + 1] ? high[out] : close[out + 1];
    double loOut = low[out] < close[out + 1] ? low[out] : close[out + 1];
    atrSum += hiIn - loIn;
    atrSum -= hiOut - loOut;
}
atrv = atrSum / (int)atrLookback;
